ter the six  months I came out still an associate  Cloud architect but with the building  blocks to be able to actually start in  the role since then I've been building  up working in front of customers and  working with my team members to actually  build the skills and enablement to  understand how to properly work with a  customer and that leaves me where I am  at today a cloud architect for AWS great  thank you so much for explaining your  journey into AWS so what are some other  ways people can become a cloud architect  I know for both of us we came from the  early career pathway which is the techu  program but for those who are interested  in becoming a cloud architect starting  with no Cloud experience how can they go  about it sure so I have a lot of  colleagues from various different  backgrounds that have joined our team  and become Cloud Architects and the two  main parts are either from becoming  another role in AWS or joining from a  consultancy background because in the  end that's what we're trying to do we're  trying to understand the customer's  problem and provide them with solutions  to be able to solve those problems and  build business value so the first one  coming from another AWS role people have  come from support roles Cloud engineer  roles and even solution Architects all  of them have built up the experience of  what AWS is and are experts in their  fields they can come along to our team  and provide Great Value into delivering  specific areas of our business and  providing specific value to what we  deliver they may need to build up and  bridge that smaller gap of how they  communicate with customers but they are  very well versed in the AWS Cloud  already on the other hand we have quite  a few people who come from a Consulting  background already those people are well  aware of how to actually engage with  customers understand their problems and  come back to them with Solutions the  area that they may need to improve on  once they get here is just understanding  what products and services AWS have in a  bit more depth because coming in and  understanding aws's culture is a really  big and important thing for us no matter  which path they come through people come  with a wide range of experience but they  still need to improve their skills to be  able to become a fully fledged Cloud  architect and naturally that comes over  time those are some really interesting  Pathways and I've definitely seen the  cloud architects in AWS come from those  so do people need to come from a  tactical background if they want to  become a cloud architect alright so one  way to build your skills and become a  cloud architect is to attend the cloud  bootcamp simply learn has launched a  cloud computing bootcamp in  collaboration with Celtic University  this bootcamp provides live classes  taught by experienced instructors and by  the end of it you receive a certificate  of completion every year the demand for  professionals with AWS Cloud skills  continues to increase and here you can  see the marker growth and average  salaries for roles in the cloud industry  the course curriculum covers a wide  range of cloud Concepts in both Azure  and AWS and you'll get to work on four  industry projects there's a three-stage  application process for The Bootcamp  where first of all you submit an  application then you wait for it to get  reviewed and selected candidates can  then begin the program within one to two  weeks the next cohort starts soon with  limited spots available so make sure you  take a look at the reviews and check out  the link to the course in the video  description below so do people need to  come from a tactical background if they  want to become a cloud Architect no  certainly not a lot of people have  joined our teams from various different  Majors back in University some from  marine biology to ethics to history the  biggest skill to become a cloud  architect is the ability to be able to  communicate with 